    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="1229" n="1215" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Korea/6–448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Jacobs</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d812-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-04T16:00:00-04:00">June 4, 1948—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>172. In recent conversation with rep of Dept, Harry of Australian Emb stated: (1)
                    that his Govt is far from satisfied with handling of Korean elections; (2) that
                    there is considerable evidence of police pressure in connection therewith; (3)
                    that in his opinion UNTCOK may take position
                    that elections were only provincial and not national <pb facs="1230" n="1216"
                        xml:id="pg1216"/> in scope; and (4) that latter point will at least be made
                    in minority report of UNTCOK.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
